{#- The heading the off-scene cast directory opens with, shared by its two tier
    sections (off_scene_cast_active.j2, off_scene_cast_known.j2).

    A file of its own rather than a copy in each of them: the directory used to
    be one template and one section, and splitting it so the two tiers could be
    measured separately (#2) must not turn a single line of instruction into
    two that can drift apart.

    Named without the leading `_` on purpose: README.md reserves that for macro
    libraries, and nothing imports this — it is rendered as prompt text, the
    way history_line.j2 and post_history.j2 are.

    NEITHER section renders it. `Section.heading` names this template and
    `context.assemble._render_sections` opens each contiguous RUN of the two
    with it, so the directory is framed however the reader's prompt layout
    orders, splits or disables its halves — one copy while they are adjacent,
    which is the catalog's order and so the default prompt. Deciding that in a
    template is what #423 was: "am I first?" is a question about the merged,
    enabled layout, and a template can only see the data. -#}
